>This paragraph has some `code` in it.</code></pre></div>","frontmatter":{"title":"Markdown Test File","description":"abc234","date":"2019-12-07T00:00:00.000Z","slug":"/pensieve/markdown-playground","tags":["Testing"]}}},"pageContext":{"language":"en","intl":{"language":"en","languages":["en","pt"],"messages":{"about":"About","experience":"Experience","education":"Education","projects":"Projects","contact":"Contact","resume_button":"Resume","hero_greeting":"Hi, my name is","hero_name":"Igor Fernando Casita.","hero_subtitle":"Junior Full-Stack Software Developer.","hero_description":"I’m a junior software developer focused on full-stack development and RESTful APIs. I have hands-on experience building real-world systems using {java}, {node}, and {python}, working with {postgres}, {docker}, and well-documented APIs using {swagger}. And on frontend, I do build systems using {react}.{br}{br}Currently pursuing an Bachelor’s degree in Systems Information at {usp}, with a planned academic progression to Bioinformatics.","about_heading":"About Me","about_p1":"Hello! My name is Igor, and I’m a junior software developer with a strong focus on backend development and building real-world systems. My interest in software development started back in 2019 when I decided to try creating games — after a few tutorials, I quickly realized that I enjoyed the problem-solving aspect of programming much more than the actual game design. Since then, I have been passionate about learning various programming languages and frameworks as well as React (DOM & Native), particularly in backend technologies like Java (Spring Boot), JavaScript/TypeScript (Node.js + Express), and Python (Django).","about_p2":"Fast-forward to today, and I’ve had the privilege of working as a volunteer at","about_p2_link":"a CPS school","about_p2_end":"My main focus these days is learning microservices architecture and cloud computing platforms like AWS.","about_p3":"Here are a few technologies I’ve been working with 